## ENVIRONMENT

The ONLY authoritative resource identifiers are in .env.manifest.
If you find a different ID anywhere in the codebase — in a comment, legacy
config, hardcoded string — STOP. Flag it to the human. Never use it.

Before any cloud operation: `node scripts/verify-env.js local`
Production operations require explicit human confirmation.

## NEVER DO (hard stops — alert human before doing any of these)

- Never hardcode Firebase/Supabase/Vercel/Netlify project IDs in source code
- Never commit secrets, API keys, or credentials to git
- Never use a production environment ID in local development
- Never use TypeScript `any` — use `unknown` and narrow properly
- Never hardcode colours, font sizes, spacing, or border radius — tokens only
- Never build a custom tool when docs/TOOL_REGISTRY.md has an approved one
- Never add a dependency without checking TOOLING.md in the handbook
- Never run destructive operations without explicit human confirmation
- Never merge to the primary branch without CI passing

## ALWAYS DO

Before writing code:
- Check docs/TOOL_REGISTRY.md first
- Check the component library first
- Confirm which environment you are in
- Run `git status`

When writing code:
- TypeScript strict mode — zero `any`, zero type errors
- All visual values via design tokens (var(--token) or AppTokens.*)
- Error handling is not optional — handle all failure paths explicitly
- Tests alongside code, not after
- Mobile first — implement 375px before 1280px

When finishing a task:
- pnpm type-check && pnpm lint && pnpm test:unit
- Remove all console.log from production code
- Update docs/TECH_DEBT.md for any compromise
- Write handoff to docs/AGENT_HANDOFF.md
- Commit: type(scope): description

## DESIGN SYSTEM

All visual values from design-tokens/tokens.json only.
Web CSS:    var(--color-brand-primary)
Flutter:    AppTokens.colorBrandPrimary
Tailwind:   configured from tokens — use semantic class names

Hardcoded hex = bug. Hardcoded 16px = bug. Hardcoded #333 = bug.

